{"name":"fire-rain-spread","tier":"B","kind":"tick","seed":123,"dimension":"overworld","world":"empty","ticks":1600,"mob_spawning":"none","comment":"The rain terms of BlockFire.updateTick (BlockFire.java:61 and the spread loop, :85-108) under steady rain (set_weather at t=0: raining, rain_time 30000, thunder off; isRaining from about t=21; every column is a rainy biome at seed 123). A stone platform and a stone roof at y=63 over x,z -12..12, open only at one-block holes. Nine fires on netherrack (BlockFire.java:56: rain never puts them out, so they tick every 40 ticks for the whole run), set at t=40 at x,z in {-8,0,8}, each ringed by wool (35) at Chebyshev distance 2 on y=61, so the eight air blocks around each fire are spread targets. Holes over the fires at (-8,-8), (0,-8), (8,-8), (-8,0) and (0,0) make the fire's own column rained on: the target at (x+1, z) is blocked by the -x term, those at (x-1, z), (x, z-1) and (x, z+1) by the +x, +z and -z terms, and those at (x+1, z+-1) only through the vanilla bug that tests (x'-1, y', z) with the fire's z instead of the target's (BlockFire.java:97). Holes over the four corner targets of the fires at (8,0), (-8,8), (0,8) and (8,8) block each corner through its own term alone. Two plain fires on wool under lone holes at (-4,62,4) and (4,62,-4) go out at their first tick through the fire's own term only (BlockFire.java:61). A target that does catch is under the roof, so it burns on into the wool. block_box every 20, scheduled_ticks every 20, rng_state every tick.",
